SM-T715 tablet: no do-not-disturb poll, no modem or call watcher.

The home screen's quick toggles asked the notification service for
do-not-disturb with `qs ipc ... notifications dndState` when they appeared,
after each tap and every 30 s: a qs client process and an IPC round trip
each time. Omarchy's notification service already keeps the setting in
~/.local/state/omarchy/notifications.json ({"version": 3, "dnd": ...},
saved by its FileView 200 ms after every change, with an atomic rename),
so the toggles now watch that file, as the bar watches its
notifications-seen mark; no file means do-not-disturb was never turned on.
Off the device, Quickshell 0.3.2's FileView followed six alternating
atomic writes in a row, the first of which created the file. Upstream
paused the 30 s poll while the widget is hidden since 0.2.44 (its `shown`
property); the file watch needs no timer at all, hidden or not.

The status bar started omamobile-cell-watch and omamobile-call-watch
--observe at every shell start. The tablet build ships neither (no modem,
no omatel), so each start only logged "Process failed to start". They now
run only while the bar's `cellWatch` / `callWatch` setting in shell.json is
true (default off); plugins/README.md lists both. Against omarchy-mobile
87b8395 (omamobile-shell 0.2.94), packages/omamobile-shell (applied with
patch -p1 in that directory, after 0001 and 0002; renumbered from 0004,
the drawer patch it followed is upstream now).

